  "title": "2011 Portuguese legislative election",
  "summary": "The early election of 5 June 2011 was held six weeks after the request for external assistance and under a memorandum the two largest opposition parties had already signed. The Social Democrats won it under Pedro Passos Coelho, took seventeen of the twenty districts and formed a coalition with the CDS holding about 56 per cent of the seats; turnout was under sixty per cent. The government it produced carried the three-year programme to its end in May 2014, and everything the adjustment did — the tax rises of 2013, the cuts the Constitutional Court struck down, the emigration — was done by it. It is in the atlas as the mandate the adjustment was carried out under.",
